---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';

const seo = {
  description: "Dzaleka Online Services Open Data License. Learn how you can freely use, share, and adapt our publicly available datasets and resources.",
  type: "website",
  canonical: "https://services.dzaleka.com/open-license",
  title: "Open Data License"
};
---
<MainLayout 
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description} 
  type={seo.type} 
  canonical={seo.canonical} 
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-gray-50">
    {/* Hero Section */}
    <div class="border-b border-gray-200 bg-white py-12 lg:py-16">
      <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 mb-6">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-700" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 11c0 3.517-1.009 6.799-2.753 9.571m-3.44-2.04l.054-.09A13.916 13.916 0 008 11a4 4 0 118 0c0 1.017-.07 2.019-.203 3m-2.118 6.844A21.88 21.88 0 0015.171 17m3.839 1.132c.645-2.266.99-4.659.99-7.132A8 8 0 008 4.07M3 15.364c.64-1.319 1-2.8 1-4.364 0-1.457.39-2.823 1.07-4" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700">Open Data License</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900">
            Open Data License
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
            Facilitating and encouraging the free reuse of publicly available data.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Content Section */}
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-8">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <h2>1. Introduction to Open Data</h2>
          <p>
            Designated public datasets and API endpoints from Dzaleka Online Services are available under an Open Data License for research, software development, reporting, and community use.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Your Rights (The License)</h2>
          <p>
            Unless explicitly stated otherwise on a specific dataset or file, the public data provided by Dzaleka Online Services is licensed under the <strong>Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)</strong> license or the <strong>Open Data Commons Attribution License (ODC-BY)</strong>. This means you are free to:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Share:</strong> Copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format.</li>
            <li><strong>Adapt:</strong> Remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose, even commercially.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. Your Obligations (Attribution)</h2>
          <p>
            The freedom to use and adapt our data comes with one primary requirement: <strong>Attribution</strong>. We ask that you:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Give appropriate credit to "Dzaleka Online Services".</li>
            <li>Provide a direct link to the license and the original dataset source.</li>
            <li>Indicate clearly if you made any changes or modifications to the original data.</li>
            <li>Do not suggest in any way that Dzaleka Online Services endorses you or your specific use of the data.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. Exceptions & Privacy Protections</h2>
          <p>
            Note that "Open Data" does <strong>not</strong> apply to personal information. Our <a href="/privacy" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 underline">Privacy Policy</a> sets strict boundaries on data sharing. The Open Data License only applies to explicitly marked, anonymized, and aggregated statistical data, or public directory information that users have explicitly consented to make public.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Encouraging Reuse</h2>
          <p>
            We actively encourage hackathons, academic researchers, and digital humanitarians to utilize our data to find solutions for the Dzaleka community. By opening our data, we aim to eliminate silos and foster an ecosystem of transparency and innovation.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have built something using our open data, we'd love to see it! Or, if you need clarification on what data falls under this license, reach out to us at:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Email: info@mail.dzaleka.com</li>
            <li>Subject: Open Data Usage Inquiry</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 text-center">
          <a
            href="/data"
            class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 border border-transparent text-base font-medium rounded-md shadow-sm text-white bg-primary-600 hover:bg-primary-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2 focus:ring-primary-500"
          >
            View public data
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    @apply text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4;
  }
  .prose p {
    @apply text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4;
  }
  .prose ul {
    @apply text-gray-700 mb-6 list-disc list-inside space-y-2;
  }
</style>
